WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.009
Avengers: Endgame gave fans everything they
were hoping for.

00:00:03.009 --> 00:00:04.240
Well, almost everything.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.940
To the surprise of many, Marvel decided to
do away with a time-honored tradition and

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.140
didn't include any mid or post-credits scenes
in Endgame.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.520
Here are the reasons why.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.400
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.199
As you're no doubt aware, a Spider-Man: Homecoming
sequel is right around the corner.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:20.960
"So nice to finally meet you, Spider-Man."

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.220
Marvel president Kevin Feige has confirmed
that Spider-Man: Far From Home takes place

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.880
shortly after the events of Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.029
Producer Amy Pascal went one step further,
revealing that the highly anticipated Spidey

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:35.520
sequel is kicking off just minutes after the
fourth Avengers flick.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.700
Seeing as Spider-Man: Far From Home is officially
the end of Phase 3, it sounds like Marvel

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.800
is saving a huge Phase 4 post-credit reveal
for that movie.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.840
As Feige told ComicBook.com:

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.720
"There's a tremendous amount of potential
and a tremendous amount of additional characters

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:52.100
and storylines and groups of characters that
we're going to keep playing with."

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.410
If we're lucky, we'll get our first proper
glimpse at these new characters during the

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.680
closing credits for Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.440
Endgame is shaping up to be the end of an
era, and the death of more than one original

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.090
Avenger makes it the heaviest Marvel movie
to date.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.549
The studio clearly wanted viewers to take
in the three-hour movie before they began

00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:09.140
looking forward to what's coming next.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.409
As The Verge's Chaim Gartenberg wrote:

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:15.779
"With Endgame, it's time to pay the check
and end the story instead of endlessly escalating

00:01:15.779 --> 00:01:17.320
and teasing the next thing."

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.160
While there was no post-credits scene to speak
of, Marvel didn't leave us totally hanging.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.200
Fans who were willing to sit through the lengthy
credits were rewarded with a little surprise:

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.520
a huge Marvel logo and a clanking sound.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.880
[clang, clang, clang, clang]

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.479
Sure, this probably left a lot of viewers
scratching their heads, but fans who have

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.960
been with the MCU from the very beginning
quickly recognized the sound.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.709
[clang, clang, clang, clang]

00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:50.060
As if to reinforce the idea that every film
we'd seen was building up to this film, Marvel

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.639
decided to make the final moment in the credits
a nod to the Marvel movie that started it

00:01:53.639 --> 00:01:55.889
all: 2008's Iron Man.

00:01:55.889 --> 00:02:00.030
It's the sound of Tony Stark cobbling together
his Iron Man shell from the first Iron Man.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.210
While Endgame was clearly something of a swansong
for some of the original Avengers, the man

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.759
of the hour was Tony Stark.

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:09.659
He started it all in that cave, and he ended
it when he snapped Thanos and his army out

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:10.520
of existence.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.600
There's been plenty of news regarding the
future of the Marvel Cinematic Universe post-Phase

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.880
3, with Marvel president Kevin Feige having
discussed a number of projects that the studio

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.420
currently has in the pipeline.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.300
Feige has suggested the Eternals will play
a big role in the plot going forward.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.010
He's also revealed that an appearance from
Ms. Marvel - otherwise known as Pakistani

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:32.490
American teen Kamala Khan - is a distinct
possibility in the near future.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.490
Feige told the BBC,

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:36.159
"[The character is] definitely sort of in
the works."

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:40.079
The producer has been purposefully vague as
far as details are concerned, and for very

00:02:40.079 --> 00:02:44.069
good reason: The fact of the matter is, Phase
4 is still very much up in the air.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:47.880
With that in mind, creating a post-credits
scene for Avengers: Endgame would've been

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.260
especially tricky.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.469
Guess we'll just have to wait and see what
the future has in store,.

00:02:51.469 --> 00:02:53.299
As a wise man once said:

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:55.599
"Sometimes patience is the key to victory.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:57.480
Sometimes it leads to very little."

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.840
That's… very true.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.920
As for what Phase 4 has in store, guess we'll
just have to patiently wait until Spider-Man:

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.730
Far From Home hits theaters on July 5th, 2019.

